//! Exact 2-adic and Mahler analysis for the aperiodic survivor itinerary
//! generated by the uniform morphism `mu(1) = 1110`, `mu(0) = 1101`.
//!
//! Scope and epistemic discipline:
//! * The infinite parity word `w = limit of mu^j(1)` defines a unique 2-adic
//!   integer `x(w)` in `Z_2`, not a demonstrated divergent positive integer.
//! * Every finite prefix `w_<K` is realized by positive integers in one
//!   residue class modulo `2^K`, even when no positive integer realizes the
//!   infinite word (illustrated by the periodic control `(1110)^infinity`,
//!   whose unique 2-adic seed is `-19/11`).
//! * Coefficient noncrossing (`3^(r_k) > 2^k` for all `k >= 1`) is a symbolic
//!   regime (`tau(w) = +infinity`); without assuming the Coefficient Stopping
//!   Time conjecture (CST), hypothetical nonconvergent positive orbits are not
//!   automatically restricted to this regime.
//! * All computations use exact arbitrary-precision integers (`BigUint` and
//!   `BigInt`). No floating-point arithmetic is used anywhere.

use num_bigint::{BigInt, BigUint};
use num_traits::{One, Pow, Zero};
use serde::Serialize;

use crate::collatz;
use crate::hypothesis::Status;
use crate::prefix::{closed_form_offset, residue_by_inverse, AffineMap, Cylinder, ParityPrefix};
use crate::serde_dec;

